hermes v2026.9.14 (0.21.3): with the Camofox backend the agent cannot get
a file that a page download starts.

Symptom: a click on a download link or button, a form whose answer is a
file (e.g. APKSum's reCAPTCHA form: POST, 302 to dl.apksum.com, attachment),
or a script-started blob download leaves the page as it is, and
browser_click reports success. camofox-browser does capture the file (its
Playwright download listener saves it to its temp dir and lists it under
GET /tabs/<id>/downloads), but no browser_* tool reads that route, so the
agent re-POSTs the form with fetch() from the page, which Firefox fails with
"NetworkError when attempting to fetch resource" (the cross-origin redirect
carries no CORS header), or hands the CAPTCHA token to curl.

Upstream: NousResearch/hermes-agent#52939 (open) proposes the same two
camofox calls; no PR, and main (848fc0ad) has nothing yet.

Fix: one tool, browser_downloads, offered only in Camofox mode and not
routed to an extension controller (no controller captures downloads).
Without arguments it lists the downloads of every tab of the session's own
camofox userId (popups included), oldest first, each with id, filename,
size, mime, url, status and whether this task saw it before; when none is
new it polls up to 15 s, since camofox lists a download only once saved.
save=<id>|"latest" writes the file under the working directory (the base the
file tools resolve against, TERMINAL_CWD): the target is resolved through
symlinks and must stay inside it, the page-chosen filename only supplies the
last component, an existing file is kept unless overwrite=true (the final
step is a hard link, so a file that appears meanwhile is kept as well), and
files over 50 MiB (camofox's MAX_FETCHED_RESOURCE_BYTES) are refused before
any byte moves. It asks camofox with includeData and maxBytes equal to the
chosen record's size, checks the length, and returns path, size and sha256.

The new test fails before this change: tools.browser_camofox has no
camofox_downloads.

